# solutec-lb.com: project rules

Site rule for `websites/solutec-lb.com/`. It applies in addition to the global rules in `.cursor/rules/`; where they conflict, the global rules win. Paths are relative to the site folder.

## Build verification
- After making any code changes (especially TypeScript files), run `npm run build` from inside `websites/solutec-lb.com/` to verify the build succeeds.
- If build errors occur, fix them before completing the task.

## Project structure
- All readme files go under the `readme` folder.
- CMS project with separation of concerns between admin and public.
- All JSON data files live in the `data` folder.
- All data file locations are defined in the `data-paths` constants.
- Put all tests in the `tests` directory.

## Admin structure
- For admin, all CSS goes in `admin/public/css/custom.css` and all JS in `admin/public/js/custom.js`.

## Public site structure
- For the public site, all scripts must be in `public/js` and are compiled into `script.js` with `node build-script.js`.

## Architecture
- Follow the MVC pattern: all business logic in services, request handling in controllers, and all design and presentation in views.

## Rich text editor
- The admin editor is the shared package `packages/rich-text-editor`. Refresh it with `npm run editor:build` from this site folder. Do not edit `admin/public/editor/` by hand.
- Logo colours, sampled from `public/uploads/2018/07/Solutec-Logo.bmp`: main `#8890C0`. `--color-primary` is `#6D739A` (that blue deepened to 4.6:1 on white), `--color-primary-dark` is `#525673`, and the exact sample is `--color-secondary`. These tokens live on `:root` in `admin/public/css/admin.scss` and `public/theme/solu.css`.
